{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/73408-tell-me-what-makes-you-love-geist-the-sin-eaters","id":73408,"title":"Tell me what makes you love Geist: The Sin-Eaters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-16T15:07:21-08:00","id":73408,"title":"Tell me what makes you love Geist: The Sin-Eaters","content":"So recently (relatively speaking) I was directed through the M:tAw forum to Dave Brookshaw's Broken Diamond AP, and went on from there to read his Soul Cage AP and now his third M:tAw AP. Before reading these, I had a cursory interest in Mage, but it didn't really grip me until reading these APs made it come alive.<br /> <br /> So now I'm looking into some of the other lines, and hoping the fans of those lines can open my eyes to their wonders, too.<br /> <br /> What do you love about Geist: The Sin-Eaters? Tell me about it! A character you love, or one of those perfect roleplaying moments you've had. A post you read that perfectly encapsulated everything you felt about the game. An AP that captured your imagination. Anything!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2286-indarkestknight","name":"indarkestknight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T16:33:54-08:00","id":73438,"title":"","content":"I love ghost stories. Anything with classic haunting elements is a big plus for me.<br /> <br /> I like that Geist has such resonance with ghost stories. Every PC is someone who has returned from death to continue living, and every PC will be a little different as to why they chose to. The Geist also makes an interesting element to the whole thing, the odd spirit who returns them from the grave. The relationship between character and spirit, more complex then the more antagonistic relationships automatic in most similar games (Wraith, Deadlands) though without the power struggle mechanics. Not bashing power struggle mechanics but it is an interesting change.<br /> <br /> It is also, as WW/OPP games go, less of a &quot;you are part of the hierarchy&quot; game. (not that I have a problem with such, mind!) The game seems focused on interactions with the dead and living, less so with other Sin-Eaters, based on their rarity and the very individual natures of their Krewes. It still is easy to have a city full of Sin-Eaters if one wishes, but it is less a part of the intrinsic game than, say, Changeling or Vampire.<br /> <br /> For me, the draw is you are essentially playing a living ghost. Your powers have a decidedly ghostly cast to them, and you are still drawn to haunted and morbid places. There is a lot of symbolic elements to how the powers work, such as the keys unlocking manifestations, that makes the game particularly drip with atmosphere. The powers are often ghastly or frightening without going overboard on being horrific as well, they do the theme with gusto.<br /> <br /> The biggest downside is that given the exponential nature of the powers, there is going to be a lot of crossover with other players. In a long running game it is difficult not to have most of your powers also possessed by one or another different PC (though not an issue with Ceremonies). Power level is also on the high side, but I run Scion this is nothing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Boneyard can be a trap for an unprepared GM as well.<br /> <br /> If you enjoy APs, I will note I have three, including one for Geist, in my signature. Balance of Shadows is about four years old, past session 100 three weeks ago, if you want to see a long running chronicle. There is also a historical shorter one on the forum.<br /> <br /> I'd be glad to expound if you wish, but in short, Geist is a spooky little game about people who have risen from the grave and now walk with the dead. Their existence is full of ghosts and they can choose to be avengers or psychopomps or profiteers, or all three, in a game that can have moments of The Crow or Nightmare Before Christmas, or The Innocents, or Beetlejuice...possibly in the same session.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T19:00:08-08:00","id":73495,"title":"","content":"As a fan of Scion (I check JSR's blog daily) and Exalted (most of my posts in the last forum were on the Exalted forum), power level being on the high side doesn't particularly bug me, either.<br /> <br /> By all means, expound away!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2286-indarkestknight","name":"indarkestknight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T09:06:15-08:00","id":73742,"title":"","content":"I've always been a fan of &quot;dead man walking&quot; type stories (The Crow, Robocop, etc.), so that part has been attractive to me from the beginning. I also love how radically different it is from any other WoD game, both mechanically and thematically. The breadth of ability that Key + Manifestation gives Bound is staggering, almost on par with the utility of Mage Arcana. But more than that, Bound are characters who WANT TO LIVE. Their force of will, their desire to keep going, is what allows the Bargain to take place. And if they go about their Sin-Eating work, they are helping not only rid the world of potentially dangerous ghosts, but are freeing the ghosts from their entrapment on Earth and letting the move on to whatever lies beyond (whether that's indeed A Better Place or not is open to debate, but still.) It's the most hopeful gameline by default in the nWoD, without coming across as out of place. Finally, the idea of symbiosis, of Geist and Bound being so intimately connected, is another concept that's always fascinated me in fiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T14:36:44-08:00","id":73889,"title":"","content":"I think what really sets Geist apart for me personally and makes it truly come alive, is the fact that it is the World of Darkness game most closely related and steeped in death and the morbid, but is also the one to celebrate and cherish life the most. In spite of all the Necromantic and spectral power that the Sin-Eaters posses, they don't sit around and pout all day, about the inevitability of death, and the pointlessness of it all. They have seen the ashen gates, and returned to life reinvigorated by their experience.<br /> Having been through a few rough patches myself, (Lets be honest, who hasn't?) this type of &quot;Looking into the abyss, and coming through stronger on the other side&quot;, really speaks to me. I really love life. I do. I love the sounds, the smells, the people, the colors and the limitless wealth of knowledge to be had. I even love the assholes, because they make me cherish all the friends i have all the more. However, I'm still a realist. I don't run off seeking adventure or &quot;true love&quot; in places where logic dictate i wont find it. Geist is the only WoD game that i feel really agrees with me on all that. It basically says &quot;Yes. Everything is going to die. And that's all right, because it wont die today. And today, we celebrate that!.&quot; <br /> Its simultaneously the most morbid and grim, as well as the most happy and posetive. And i really love it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T16:27:23-08:00","id":75309,"title":"","content":"while this has been said before Giest is a story about second chances you died once and now you have the willpower to come out of it with a second life. They don't hate their power they love it unlike the other taglines involving supernatural angst these guys jumped at the call to start a new life and that's what I love about Giest you are strong enough to survive a terrible death and come back from it not only with a new life but a new happy take on life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T00:38:48-08:00","id":75470,"title":"","content":"Basically all the reasons above, and also due to the way the game is written, the 'bad guys' are that way because of ideology, rather than divine metaphysics (which WW/OP has a tendency to lean on)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T02:13:41-08:00","id":75487,"title":"","content":"There is that. Though Vampire tends to avoid that too. And is also one of my favorite games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T03:35:15-08:00","id":75517,"title":"","content":"It's a celebration of life, and of the things that tie us to to life and what they means to people. That's certainly the best part about the game.<br /> <br /> Plus, lots of cool powers and a rather interesting underworld.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T13:39:02-08:00","id":81761,"title":"","content":"I like it for exactly the opposite reasons of everyone except possibly Baron Samedi (and I'm beginning to think I may have read a different book than everyone else...).<br /> I love Geist exactly because its Awful, as both &quot;full of awe&quot; and &quot;terrible&quot;. Yes, you came back to a second chance, but you're living on borrowed time with a <i>thing</i> inside your head that has no conception of rational or moral judgement. It wants, for its own reasons, and now that you've made the Bargain, you have to deal with those wants. Its a game about <i>never</i> being alone, but in a more concrete way than Vampire's Beast, and more internalized than the Fae of Changeling (think about that parallel). And every time you come back, someone else dies, because that <i>thing</i> isn't done with you, even if it said it was, even if it was going to finally let you die, it needs your meat-suit to do the things it wants to do. And maybe it lets you enjoy and celebrate life because that gives it some sort of perverse thrill, or maybe you feel the need to enjoy and celebrate life because the voice sharing your body doesn't shut up about putting people in the ground; maybe celebration is your only escape. You are tortured, full of capability beyond everyone else, but at what price power? Its Goethe, and Lewis and Radcliffe all rolled into one neat little awful package with sweeping vistas in a realm of terrible damnation that will make you feel small.<br /> And yet, there you are. Doing your thing,<i>alive</i>. Because you wanted to live so badly that you <i>made </i>a deal with the Devil.<br /> That, ladies and gentlemen, is why I love Geist. Because its sublime, beautiful, and horrifying all at the same time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>ST/DM for <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCfFy7kNgMvxIR1qdzT8PzEg\" target=\"_blank\">Dice Alternatives</a><br /> Playing: <a href=\"http://causality-and-consequences.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">DtD: Causality and Consequence</a><br /> Off-Season: <a href=\"http://lifelong-educations.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">M:tAw- Lifelong Education</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/667-abenniton","name":"ABenniton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar667_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T03:08:44-08:00","id":82572,"title":"","content":"For me, Geist was the first WoD book I ever read (like, ever. I didn't even buy the core until it became apparent I needed to), and before that my gaming experience was limited to D&amp;D, which has, well, limited roleplaying opportunities. So, for me it was the gateway not just to World of Darkness, but a whole other way of approaching gaming and roleplaying.<br /> <br /> Further, I like that the game is so character-central. The others do have a focus on character, but well: werewolves are about patrolling the spirits and fighting the Pure (oversimplification, I know. If you removed those elements though, it'd be a very different game), vampires is about politicking against other vampires and avoiding hunters, changelings has the True Fae, and so on. They are, to a point at least, defined by their canon antagonists. Geist doesn't have that. The kerbori rarely if ever leave the Underworld, which a Bound can avoid without really facing too much in the way of a downside, Bound rarely oppose each other directly other than occasional territory disputes, and the rest are pretty much just the usual WoD miscellanea. So, since there's no inherent opposition to define them, Bound are instead defined within themselves, at least to a greater extent than other types of PCs. Combine that with the rich theme, interesting powers and just overall great design, really it was kind of a foregone conclusion that I'd like them the most <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T15:26:23-08:00","id":82804,"title":"","content":"Three words:<br /> <br /> Supernatural Junk Culture.<br /> <br /> Another three words:<br /> <br /> Celebrates Seeming Contradictions.<br /> <br /> That's enough for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}